MACROS(3)                   MACRO DEFINITION FUNCTIONS                MACROS(3)NAME       macros - macro definitionsSYNOPSIS       #include macros.f83       macros ( -- )       MACRO ( body size -- ) private       +body ( macro -- body) private       +size ( macro -- size) private       [macro] ( macro -- ) private       macro ( -- )       .macro ( -- )DESCRIPTION       Allows definition of macro colon definitions to reduce the       overhead of call at run-time.macros ( -- )       Vocabulary containing the macro definitions.MACRO ( body size -- ) private       Structure definition used by "macro" to keep information about       a macro code definition.+body ( macro -- body) private       Access field to pointer to code section of macro code.        Stored as a ptr.+size ( macro -- size) private       Access field to byte size of macro code.        Stored as a long.[macro] ( macro -- ) private       Run-time manager of macro definitions. If compilation state       the macro body is expanded into the current definition other-       wise the macro body is called.macro ( -- )       Used to mark a definition as a macro.                : <macro-name> <macro-definition> ; macro       Used in the same way as "immediate". The code section is not       restricted to sequential code only, control structures are       allowed as all branches are relative. Special care should be       taken if the macro definition is recursive as the result is       unpredictable..macro ( -- )       Used in the form:               .macro <macro-name>       to print internal information about the macro definition.       Use mainly for debugging purposes.SEE ALSO       forth(1), forth(2) COPYING       Copyright (C) 1989 Mikael R.K. Patel       Permission is granted to make and distribute verbatim copies       of this manual provided the copyright notice and this permission       notice are preserved on all copies.       Permission